1
00:00:00,865 --> 00:00:00,830
Sixteen.

2
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:04,110
That's how many new Jeeps were sold
in the whole of Australia in September

3
00:00:04,160 --> 00:00:05,630
2026.

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:06,870
Not sixteen a day.

5
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:07,940
Not sixteen a week.

6
00:00:07,990 --> 00:00:10,910
Sixteen in a month
across an entire country.

7
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,510
That same month, Jaguar sold zero.

8
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:16,590
Peugeot sold eighty-nine,
after losing its importer.

9
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,750
Alfa Romeo sold twenty-one.

10
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,250
And it's not just the small names.

11
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,750
Subaru was down more
than forty-two per cent.

12
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,230
Mitsubishi, down forty-one.

13
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,810
Nissan's boss has openly called
2026 the brand's low point.

14
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:33,350
Meanwhile, a Chinese brand most Aussies
couldn't name three years ago grew by

15
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,150
more than eight hundred
per cent in a single year.

16
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,370
Australia's car market is going through
the biggest shake-up in its history

17
00:00:39,420 --> 00:00:42,350
and it's happening right now, in 2026.

18
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,970
Today I'm counting down ten car brands
in serious trouble in Australia,

19
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:48,390
using the latest official sales figures.

20
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,530
And if one of these is
sitting in your driveway,

21
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:51,330
stay to the end,

22
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:54,170
because I'll explain exactly
what happens to your warranty,

23
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:58,540
your servicing and your resale value
if a brand pulls back or pulls out.

24
00:00:59,135 --> 00:01:01,265
First, let's look at
what's actually happening,

25
00:01:01,315 --> 00:01:05,145
because the numbers from
September 2026 are remarkable.

26
00:01:05,195 --> 00:01:10,385
Australians bought 108,778
new vehicles in September.

27
00:01:10,435 --> 00:01:13,005
That's up slightly on
the same month last year.

28
00:01:13,055 --> 00:01:14,685
So the market isn't collapsing.

29
00:01:14,735 --> 00:01:16,425
People are still buying cars.

30
00:01:16,475 --> 00:01:18,825
What's changing is who
they're buying from.

31
00:01:18,875 --> 00:01:20,445
Look at the brands that grew.

32
00:01:20,495 --> 00:01:22,385
BYD, up sixty-one per cent,

33
00:01:22,435 --> 00:01:24,905
now Australia's second
best-selling brand for the year.

34
00:01:24,955 --> 00:01:27,670
Geely, up 870 per cent.

35
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:30,855
Omoda and Jaecoo, up 344 per cent.

36
00:01:30,905 --> 00:01:33,665
Zeekr, up more than
sixteen hundred per cent.

37
00:01:33,715 --> 00:01:35,055
Leapmotor more than doubled.

38
00:01:35,105 --> 00:01:36,825
Now look at the other side.

39
00:01:36,875 --> 00:01:39,385
Even big, established
names went backwards.

40
00:01:39,435 --> 00:01:41,955
Kia, down nineteen and a
half per cent in September.

41
00:01:42,005 --> 00:01:44,012
Mazda, down nearly nineteen.

42
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,945
Hyundai, down twenty-two.

43
00:01:45,995 --> 00:01:47,345
Among the top ten brands,

44
00:01:47,395 --> 00:01:50,525
the only ones that grew were
Tesla and the Chinese brands.

45
00:01:50,575 --> 00:01:51,745
There's another big shift too.

46
00:01:51,795 --> 00:01:57,105
In September, electric vehicles made
up 24.2 per cent of all new car sales

47
00:01:57,155 --> 00:02:00,145
more than petrol cars, for
the second month in a row.

48
00:02:00,195 --> 00:02:03,145
Petrol sales fell thirty-six
per cent year-on-year.

49
00:02:03,195 --> 00:02:04,685
Diesel fell eighteen.

50
00:02:04,735 --> 00:02:06,945
If your range is mostly petrol and diesel,

51
00:02:06,995 --> 00:02:10,245
2026 is a very hard
year to be selling cars.

52
00:02:10,295 --> 00:02:11,745
And the market is crowded.

53
00:02:11,795 --> 00:02:16,145
Around seventy brands are now fighting
for roughly 1.2 million sales a year.

54
00:02:16,195 --> 00:02:19,765
Every sale a new brand wins comes
out of someone else's pocket.

55
00:02:19,815 --> 00:02:21,425
So why is this happening now?

56
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:23,945
There are three big
forces hitting at once.

57
00:02:23,995 --> 00:02:25,085
The first is price.

58
00:02:25,135 --> 00:02:29,005
Chinese brands arrived with well-equipped
hybrids and EVs at prices the

59
00:02:29,055 --> 00:02:31,265
established brands struggle to match.

60
00:02:31,315 --> 00:02:35,025
When a family can get a plug-in hybrid
SUV with a big screen and a long

61
00:02:35,075 --> 00:02:38,245
warranty for the same money
as a basic petrol SUV,

62
00:02:38,295 --> 00:02:40,045
plenty of them are making the switch.

63
00:02:40,095 --> 00:02:41,645
The second is fuel.

64
00:02:41,695 --> 00:02:43,945
Petrol and diesel are
losing share every month,

65
00:02:43,995 --> 00:02:47,665
and the New Vehicle Efficiency
Standard now pushes car makers to sell

66
00:02:47,715 --> 00:02:49,965
lower-emission vehicles or pay penalties.

67
00:02:50,015 --> 00:02:50,845
Brands with old,

68
00:02:50,895 --> 00:02:55,925
thirsty ranges are being squeezed from
both sides by buyers and by the rules.

69
00:02:55,975 --> 00:02:58,085
The third is the sheer number of choices.

70
00:02:58,135 --> 00:03:01,245
A few years ago, Australia
had around fifty brands.

71
00:03:01,295 --> 00:03:02,845
Now there are about seventy.

72
00:03:02,895 --> 00:03:06,305
A dealer body boss has already
warned that more brands will leave.

73
00:03:06,355 --> 00:03:07,905
The pie isn't getting much bigger.

74
00:03:07,955 --> 00:03:10,805
It's just being cut into
thinner and thinner slices.

75
00:03:10,855 --> 00:03:12,245
So who's losing the most?

76
00:03:12,295 --> 00:03:13,255
Let's count down.

77
00:03:14,932 --> 00:03:15,869
Number ten: Deepal.

78
00:03:15,919 --> 00:03:20,029
And this one proves it's not simply
old brands versus new Chinese brands.

79
00:03:20,079 --> 00:03:23,169
Deepal is an electric brand
from Chinese giant Changan,

80
00:03:23,219 --> 00:03:26,849
and it launched in Australia with
big ambitions and a stylish range.

81
00:03:26,899 --> 00:03:29,149
But 2026 has been brutal.

82
00:03:29,199 --> 00:03:33,569
By the end of May, Deepal had
sold just 594 cars for the year.

83
00:03:33,619 --> 00:03:37,949
In September, it sold sixty-three down
almost thirty-four per cent on the same

84
00:03:37,999 --> 00:03:38,769
month last year.

85
00:03:38,819 --> 00:03:42,589
A big part of that was a
stop-sale order on the E07,

86
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:47,309
a quirky electric SUV with a ute-style
tray that was meant to grab attention.

87
00:03:47,359 --> 00:03:48,909
Losing a key model to a stop-sale,

88
00:03:48,959 --> 00:03:52,809
in your first years in a brand-new
market, is about as hard as it gets.

89
00:03:52,859 --> 00:03:54,329
The lesson here is simple.

90
00:03:54,379 --> 00:03:57,309
Being Chinese and electric doesn't
guarantee success in Australia.

91
00:03:57,359 --> 00:04:01,439
The newcomers are fighting each other
just as hard as they're fighting Toyota.

92
00:04:02,292 --> 00:04:07,062
At number nine: KGM the brand most
Aussies still know as SsangYong.

93
00:04:07,112 --> 00:04:10,422
KGM changed its name after a
change of ownership in Korea,

94
00:04:10,472 --> 00:04:12,502
and it's been trying
to rebuild ever since.

95
00:04:12,552 --> 00:04:16,682
But in September 2026 it
sold just 189 vehicles,

96
00:04:16,732 --> 00:04:19,062
down thirty-seven per
cent on the year before.

97
00:04:19,112 --> 00:04:22,802
That follows a twenty-four
per cent drop across 2025.

98
00:04:22,852 --> 00:04:27,342
KGM's strength has always been tough,
good-value SUVs and the Musso ute.

99
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:31,082
The problem is that this is
exactly the space where GWM,

100
00:04:31,132 --> 00:04:36,132
LDV, BYD and now Chery are throwing
everything they've got more technology,

101
00:04:36,182 --> 00:04:40,782
plug-in hybrids, longer warranties,
and very sharp drive-away prices.

102
00:04:40,832 --> 00:04:42,882
Changing a brand's name is hard enough.

103
00:04:42,932 --> 00:04:46,092
Doing it in the most crowded market
in its history is even harder.

104
00:04:47,696 --> 00:04:48,379
Number eight: Alfa Romeo.

105
00:04:48,429 --> 00:04:49,999
Beautiful cars.

106
00:04:50,049 --> 00:04:51,339
Passionate fans.

107
00:04:51,389 --> 00:04:52,239
Almost no buyers.

108
00:04:52,289 --> 00:04:54,679
In September 2026,

109
00:04:54,729 --> 00:04:58,939
Alfa Romeo sold twenty-one cars in
Australia, down almost sixty per cent.

110
00:04:58,989 --> 00:05:02,859
Through the first five months of the
year it managed fewer than two hundred.

111
00:05:02,909 --> 00:05:06,459
Alfa sits inside Stellantis
Australia, alongside Fiat,

112
00:05:06,509 --> 00:05:09,159
Jeep and the Chinese EV brand Leapmotor.

113
00:05:09,209 --> 00:05:11,139
And that's the real question for Alfa.

114
00:05:11,189 --> 00:05:13,739
How long can a global
company justify dealers,

115
00:05:13,789 --> 00:05:17,759
parts, marketing and compliance for a
brand selling a couple of hundred cars a

116
00:05:17,809 --> 00:05:18,959
year in one market?

117
00:05:19,009 --> 00:05:23,579
For now, Alfa Romeo is still here,
and existing owners are supported.

118
00:05:23,629 --> 00:05:25,079
But with numbers like these,

119
00:05:25,129 --> 00:05:29,129
its future in Australia will be decided
in Europe, not in Aussie showrooms.

120
00:05:30,013 --> 00:05:31,963
At number seven: Suzuki.

121
00:05:32,013 --> 00:05:35,183
And 2026 has been a rough
year for the little brand.

122
00:05:35,233 --> 00:05:37,143
Suzuki built its name here on small,

123
00:05:37,193 --> 00:05:40,483
affordable, fun cars
the Swift, the Vitara,

124
00:05:40,533 --> 00:05:42,643
and of course the cult-favourite Jimny.

125
00:05:42,693 --> 00:05:47,003
But by the end of May 2026, Suzuki
sales were down twenty-two per cent.

126
00:05:47,053 --> 00:05:49,983
In September, they were
down more than thirty-nine.

127
00:05:50,033 --> 00:05:51,803
Part of it is safety ratings.

128
00:05:51,853 --> 00:05:54,583
The new Fronx small SUV launched strongly,

129
00:05:54,633 --> 00:05:58,483
then received a one-star ANCAP rating
after a rear seatbelt failure in crash

130
00:05:58,533 --> 00:05:58,943
testing.

131
00:05:58,993 --> 00:06:03,543
Sales were halted while Suzuki's
engineers investigated and months later,

132
00:06:03,593 --> 00:06:07,363
in March 2026, the investigation
was still dragging on.

133
00:06:07,413 --> 00:06:11,163
Suzuki's local boss even suggested
that an earlier one-star result for the

134
00:06:11,213 --> 00:06:14,803
Swift may have scared off as many
as one in five potential buyers.

135
00:06:14,853 --> 00:06:18,683
That's the brand's own estimate, but it
shows how much a safety score matters.

136
00:06:18,733 --> 00:06:19,973
The other part is price.

137
00:06:20,023 --> 00:06:22,503
Suzuki relies on cheap small cars,

138
00:06:22,553 --> 00:06:26,163
and that's exactly where Chinese rivals
now offer similar or better equipment

139
00:06:26,213 --> 00:06:27,003
for similar money.

140
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:30,673
Even the Jimny was down twelve
per cent in the first five months.

141
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:33,849
Number six: Volkswagen.

142
00:06:33,899 --> 00:06:35,289
This one surprises people,

143
00:06:35,339 --> 00:06:38,369
because Volkswagen is one of the
biggest car makers on the planet.

144
00:06:38,419 --> 00:06:40,849
But in Australia, it's shrinking fast.

145
00:06:40,899 --> 00:06:46,109
VW sold about 29,000 vehicles in
2025, down more than twenty per cent.

146
00:06:46,159 --> 00:06:49,949
By the end of May 2026 it was
down another seventeen per cent.

147
00:06:49,999 --> 00:06:51,349
And in September,

148
00:06:51,399 --> 00:06:57,309
Volkswagen sold 1,599 cars down almost
thirty-seven per cent on the same month

149
00:06:57,359 --> 00:06:58,109
last year.

150
00:06:58,159 --> 00:07:00,509
Look inside those numbers
and it gets worse.

151
00:07:00,559 --> 00:07:03,789
In the first five months, the
T-Roc was down fifty-six per cent.

152
00:07:03,839 --> 00:07:06,129
The T-Cross, down forty-nine.

153
00:07:06,179 --> 00:07:08,609
The Amarok ute, down
more than thirty-three.

154
00:07:08,659 --> 00:07:10,349
At a launch event in May,

155
00:07:10,399 --> 00:07:12,279
Volkswagen's passenger
car boss in Australia,

156
00:07:12,329 --> 00:07:15,249
Piergiorgio Minto, said
something very telling.

157
00:07:15,299 --> 00:07:16,629
Paraphrasing his point:

158
00:07:16,679 --> 00:07:19,249
once you're selling fewer than
ten thousand vehicles a year,

159
00:07:19,299 --> 00:07:20,449
you're a niche brand.

160
00:07:20,499 --> 00:07:23,209
And he made it clear Volkswagen
doesn't want to be niche.

161
00:07:23,259 --> 00:07:25,429
The brand admits it has
had gaps in its range,

162
00:07:25,479 --> 00:07:29,109
and that new models have often reached
Australia years after their global

163
00:07:29,159 --> 00:07:30,129
debut.

164
00:07:30,179 --> 00:07:34,189
There's a new-generation T-Roc and
more hybrids and plug-ins on the way.

165
00:07:34,239 --> 00:07:35,399
But the clock is ticking.

166
00:07:36,271 --> 00:07:38,301
Quick one before we get into the top five.

167
00:07:38,351 --> 00:07:42,101
If you're finding this useful, hit
subscribe and turn on notifications.

168
00:07:42,151 --> 00:07:45,341
Every week we break down what's really
happening in the Australian car market,

169
00:07:45,391 --> 00:07:49,221
using real 2026 sales data not rumours.

170
00:07:49,271 --> 00:07:52,561
And tell me in the comments: do you
own one of the brands on this list?

171
00:07:52,611 --> 00:07:53,801
Would you buy another one?

172
00:07:53,851 --> 00:07:54,991
I read every comment.

173
00:07:55,715 --> 00:07:57,665
Number five: Subaru.

174
00:07:57,715 --> 00:08:00,525
Subaru has some of the most
loyal owners in the country,

175
00:08:00,575 --> 00:08:03,225
especially in the bush and
among outdoor families.

176
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:05,645
But 2026 has been tough.

177
00:08:05,695 --> 00:08:09,212
Sales for the first five months were
down twenty-two per cent almost four

178
00:08:09,262 --> 00:08:11,585
thousand fewer cars than the year before.

179
00:08:11,635 --> 00:08:16,765
In September, Subaru sold 2,009 vehicles,
down more than forty-two per cent.

180
00:08:16,815 --> 00:08:22,005
To put that in perspective, Subaru
sold more than 46,000 cars in 2023.

181
00:08:22,055 --> 00:08:24,058
Now it has slipped behind Geely,

182
00:08:24,108 --> 00:08:27,685
Omoda Jaecoo and even
BMW on the sales charts.

183
00:08:27,735 --> 00:08:29,745
Subaru's importer says
this is partly planned.

184
00:08:29,795 --> 00:08:34,265
Managing director Blair Read described
it as a rationalisation of the range

185
00:08:34,315 --> 00:08:36,905
the Liberty is gone,
STI models are paused,

186
00:08:36,955 --> 00:08:40,605
and the Forester and Outback were
both replaced within twelve months.

187
00:08:40,655 --> 00:08:44,685
Subaru says it will have nine models
in showrooms by the end of 2026,

188
00:08:44,735 --> 00:08:46,745
five of them hybrid or electric.

189
00:08:46,795 --> 00:08:47,385
That's the plan.

190
00:08:47,435 --> 00:08:51,725
But in a market where buyers are
rushing to cheaper electrified SUVs,

191
00:08:51,775 --> 00:08:54,335
Subaru needs that new
range to work and quickly.

192
00:08:56,134 --> 00:08:57,165
At number four: Nissan.

193
00:08:57,215 --> 00:09:00,605
Ten years ago, Nissan was one of
the biggest players in Australia.

194
00:09:00,655 --> 00:09:03,905
In 2012 it sold almost
eighty thousand cars here.

195
00:09:03,955 --> 00:09:07,625
In 2026, it's fighting for
survival on the sales charts.

196
00:09:07,675 --> 00:09:08,985
To the end of July,

197
00:09:09,035 --> 00:09:14,325
Nissan had delivered 15,445 vehicles
down almost thirty-four per cent.

198
00:09:14,375 --> 00:09:16,905
The Navara ute was down
forty-nine per cent.

199
00:09:16,955 --> 00:09:20,365
The Qashqai was down a staggering
seventy-three and a half per cent.

200
00:09:20,415 --> 00:09:23,765
Even the X-Trail, Nissan's
best seller, was down fifteen.

201
00:09:23,815 --> 00:09:27,225
In September, the brand was
still down thirty per cent.

202
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:31,085
Nissan has already cut the Juke and
the Pathfinder from its local range,

203
00:09:31,135 --> 00:09:33,705
and the new Leaf has been
postponed indefinitely.

204
00:09:33,755 --> 00:09:36,585
Globally, the company has been
through a massive restructure,

205
00:09:36,635 --> 00:09:38,785
with factory closures and job cuts.

206
00:09:38,835 --> 00:09:40,445
And here's the remarkable part.

207
00:09:40,495 --> 00:09:43,185
Nissan's new Oceania boss, Steve Milette,

208
00:09:43,235 --> 00:09:46,325
has said publicly that
2026 is the low point,

209
00:09:46,375 --> 00:09:49,125
and that he expects growth
to return from next year.

210
00:09:49,175 --> 00:09:51,245
The plan includes hybrid X-Trails,

211
00:09:51,295 --> 00:09:51,685
the new Patrol,

212
00:09:51,735 --> 00:09:56,785
and possibly plug-in hybrid utes and
SUVs built with Chinese partner Dongfeng.

213
00:09:56,835 --> 00:09:59,265
When a brand's own boss
calls this year the bottom,

214
00:09:59,315 --> 00:10:01,735
you know just how hard 2026 has been.

215
00:10:03,418 --> 00:10:04,510
Number three: Mitsubishi.

216
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:08,430
Mitsubishi used to be the smart value
choice for Aussie families and tradies.

217
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:11,730
In 2018 it sold almost 85,000 cars here.

218
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:15,350
In 2024 it was the fifth
best-selling brand in the country.

219
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:19,550
By the end of May 2026, Mitsubishi was
down more than twenty-six per cent.

220
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:20,610
And in September,

221
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:25,930
it sold 2,769 vehicles down
forty-one and a half per cent.

222
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:26,950
What went wrong?

223
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,210
The range shrank.

224
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:31,550
The Pajero Sport and the Eclipse
Cross were dropped in 2025,

225
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,670
partly because of new safety rules.

226
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:36,190
The new ASX is now a rebadged Renault,

227
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,210
with a much higher starting price,

228
00:10:38,260 --> 00:10:42,690
and it sold just 695 units in
the first five months of 2026.

229
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:45,170
The Outlander, Mitsubishi's best seller,

230
00:10:45,220 --> 00:10:49,030
now faces plug-in hybrid
rivals like the BYD Sealion 6.

231
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:52,910
In fact, the only Mitsubishi not going
backwards this year has been the Triton

232
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:53,590
ute.

233
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,190
And here's the core problem.

234
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:57,390
Mitsubishi's whole identity was value.

235
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,810
But in 2026,

236
00:10:58,860 --> 00:11:02,690
the value end of the market belongs
to Chinese brands with bigger ranges,

237
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:05,910
more technology, and in
many cases lower prices.

238
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:11,090
A new boss started in January, and a new
Pajero and a small EV are on the way.

239
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:12,560
Mitsubishi needs them badly.

240
00:11:13,366 --> 00:11:14,856
Number two: Jeep.

241
00:11:14,906 --> 00:11:18,496
If you want to see what a long,
slow decline looks like, this is it.

242
00:11:18,546 --> 00:11:19,476
Remember the hook?

243
00:11:19,526 --> 00:11:23,776
Sixteen Jeeps sold in September
2026, down eighty-five per cent.

244
00:11:23,826 --> 00:11:26,056
Across the first eight months of the year,

245
00:11:26,106 --> 00:11:29,236
Jeep sold just 378 vehicles in Australia.

246
00:11:29,286 --> 00:11:33,056
Back in 2014, Jeep sold more
than thirty thousand cars here.

247
00:11:33,106 --> 00:11:36,636
That's a fall of around ninety-nine
per cent in just over a decade.

248
00:11:36,686 --> 00:11:40,076
The once-popular Grand
Cherokee was axed in 2025.

249
00:11:40,126 --> 00:11:43,976
The dealer network has shrunk from
more than seventy to around forty-four,

250
00:11:44,026 --> 00:11:47,656
and some dealers have said publicly they
feared the brand was being run down.

251
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:51,596
But there's a twist, and it
only came out in October 2026.

252
00:11:51,646 --> 00:11:55,836
Jeep's parent company, Stellantis, has
partnered with Chinese giant Dongfeng.

253
00:11:55,886 --> 00:11:59,036
Reports say future Jeep and Peugeot
models could be built in China,

254
00:11:59,086 --> 00:12:00,816
in Dongfeng's Wuhan factory,

255
00:12:00,866 --> 00:12:05,036
as plug-in hybrids or EVs
aiming for sharper prices.

256
00:12:05,086 --> 00:12:08,496
Stellantis says it will share Australian
details "at the appropriate time".

257
00:12:08,546 --> 00:12:12,616
So the brand famous for American
off-roaders may end up being rescued by

258
00:12:12,666 --> 00:12:14,016
Chinese manufacturing.

259
00:12:14,066 --> 00:12:16,606
That tells you everything about
where this market is heading.

260
00:12:17,364 --> 00:12:19,254
And number one: Peugeot.

261
00:12:19,304 --> 00:12:21,074
In July 2026,

262
00:12:21,124 --> 00:12:24,714
Inchcape the company that imported and
distributed Peugeot in Australia for

263
00:12:24,764 --> 00:12:28,154
almost a decade announced it
was walking away from the brand.

264
00:12:28,204 --> 00:12:29,774
The numbers explain why.

265
00:12:29,824 --> 00:12:34,794
Peugeot sold just 373 vehicles
to the end of May 2026,

266
00:12:34,844 --> 00:12:38,614
down thirty-five per cent, and more
than half of those were commercial vans.

267
00:12:38,664 --> 00:12:42,364
In all of 2025, it sold 1,350.

268
00:12:42,414 --> 00:12:47,354
Back in 2007, Peugeot
sold 8,807 cars here.

269
00:12:47,404 --> 00:12:50,474
And in September 2026,
it sold eighty-nine.

270
00:12:50,524 --> 00:12:55,634
A facelifted 308 hatch was meant to
arrive in the first half of 2026.

271
00:12:55,684 --> 00:12:56,814
It never came.

272
00:12:56,864 --> 00:12:58,854
Instead, right after the announcement,

273
00:12:58,904 --> 00:13:02,704
Peugeot slashed prices across its
passenger range drive-away discounts from

274
00:13:02,754 --> 00:13:06,814
six thousand dollars all
the way up to $14,718.

275
00:13:06,864 --> 00:13:11,614
The flagship 5008 GT hybrid
dropped by ten thousand dollars.

276
00:13:11,664 --> 00:13:14,594
Stellantis insists Peugeot
is not leaving Australia.

277
00:13:14,644 --> 00:13:17,834
It says the brand has a strong
future here and will continue after a

278
00:13:17,884 --> 00:13:19,874
transition period of around a year.

279
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:23,814
And as we just saw, Peugeot is also
part of that new Dongfeng plan.

280
00:13:23,864 --> 00:13:28,414
But Inchcape already dropped Peugeot's
sister brand, Citroën, back in 2024.

281
00:13:28,464 --> 00:13:31,974
Losing your importer is the clearest
warning sign a brand can get and that's

282
00:13:32,024 --> 00:13:34,104
why Peugeot is number one on this list.

283
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:38,310
And a bonus, because this
one is almost unbelievable.

284
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:42,190
Jaguar sold zero cars in
Australia in September 2026.

285
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:42,970
Not a few.

286
00:13:43,020 --> 00:13:43,790
Zero.

287
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:47,570
That's because Jaguar stopped selling
new petrol cars here on the 31st of

288
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:52,510
December 2025, as it reinvents itself
as an all-electric luxury brand.

289
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:55,530
Its new EVs are expected to cost
around three hundred thousand dollars

290
00:13:55,580 --> 00:13:59,350
locally, and there's still no
confirmed Australian launch date.

291
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:03,410
Jaguar's local retailers are still
servicing cars and honouring warranties.

292
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:04,310
But for now,

293
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:07,550
a brand with nearly a century of
history is selling nothing new in this

294
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,400
country.

295
00:14:08,975 --> 00:14:13,105
So what happens if you own a car from
a brand that pulls back or pulls out?

296
00:14:13,155 --> 00:14:16,085
First, the good news:
you're not left on your own.

297
00:14:16,135 --> 00:14:17,965
When Citroën stopped selling new cars,

298
00:14:18,015 --> 00:14:21,305
its importer confirmed it would keep
honouring warranties on cars already

299
00:14:21,355 --> 00:14:22,285
sold.

300
00:14:22,335 --> 00:14:24,705
Peugeot owners are being told
the same during the transition,

301
00:14:24,755 --> 00:14:29,465
and Jaguar retailers are still
servicing and honouring warranty claims.

302
00:14:29,515 --> 00:14:31,565
Second, the law is on your side.

303
00:14:31,615 --> 00:14:33,545
Under the Australian Consumer Law,

304
00:14:33,595 --> 00:14:36,965
manufacturers and importers must make
spare parts and repair facilities

305
00:14:37,015 --> 00:14:39,825
available for a reasonable
time after you buy.

306
00:14:39,875 --> 00:14:42,485
That doesn't disappear just
because sales slow down.

307
00:14:42,535 --> 00:14:44,935
Third, the real risk is resale value.

308
00:14:44,985 --> 00:14:48,845
Cars from brands that are shrinking or
look like they might leave usually lose

309
00:14:48,895 --> 00:14:50,005
value faster.

310
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:52,925
If you're buying one, use
that to negotiate hard.

311
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:57,105
Some of the biggest discounts in 2026
have come from exactly these brands.

312
00:14:57,155 --> 00:15:00,725
And if you're selling, it may pay
to sell sooner rather than later.

313
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:03,405
Finally, before you buy any
car from a smaller brand,

314
00:15:03,455 --> 00:15:04,705
ask the dealer three things.

315
00:15:04,755 --> 00:15:07,325
How long is the warranty,
and who backs it?

316
00:15:07,375 --> 00:15:08,965
Where is the nearest service centre?

317
00:15:09,015 --> 00:15:11,225
And how quickly can they get common parts?

318
00:15:11,275 --> 00:15:14,025
The answers will tell you how
much risk you're taking on.

319
00:15:14,075 --> 00:15:15,805
And one more thing worth remembering:

320
00:15:15,855 --> 00:15:18,625
a struggling brand isn't
automatically a bad car.

321
00:15:18,675 --> 00:15:22,165
Some of the brands on this list
make genuinely excellent vehicles.

322
00:15:22,215 --> 00:15:26,325
A Subaru Forester or a Volkswagen Golf
doesn't suddenly become a worse car

323
00:15:26,375 --> 00:15:28,385
because fewer people are buying them.

324
00:15:28,435 --> 00:15:30,665
But when sales fall, dealers close,

325
00:15:30,715 --> 00:15:33,085
service networks shrink,
and resale values soften.

326
00:15:33,135 --> 00:15:37,265
So the question isn't just "is this a
good car?" It's "will this brand still

327
00:15:37,315 --> 00:15:38,855
look after me in five years?

328
00:15:39,707 --> 00:15:44,697
That's ten car brands in serious trouble
in Australia in 2026 plus one that's

329
00:15:44,747 --> 00:15:46,637
currently selling nothing at all.

330
00:15:46,687 --> 00:15:48,497
Which one do you think leaves first?

331
00:15:48,547 --> 00:15:51,057
Tell me in the comments, and
I'll pin the best answer.

332
00:15:51,107 --> 00:15:52,457
If you got value from this,

333
00:15:52,507 --> 00:15:53,737
hit like and subscribe,

334
00:15:53,787 --> 00:15:55,977
because this shake-up
is only getting started,

335
00:15:56,027 --> 00:15:58,157
and we'll be tracking every month of it.

336
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:01,257
And if you want to know what to do if
your brand-new car turns out to be a

337
00:16:01,307 --> 00:16:04,997
lemon, the next video shows how Aussies
are fighting back against faulty new

338
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:06,537
cars and winning.

339
00:16:06,587 --> 00:16:07,387
See you there.
